{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Speak to all the congregation… You shall be holy.</b> After He caused His Shekhinah to dwell among Israel to sanctify them for eternal life — as was the intent in His saying וְאַתֶּם תִּהְיוּ לִי מַמְלֶכֶת כֹּהֲנִים וְגוֹי קָדוֹשׁ (Exodus 19:6), and in His saying כִּי אֲנִי ה׳ הַמַּעֲלֶה אֶתְכֶם מֵאֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם לִהְיוֹת לָכֶם לֵאלֹהִים וִהְיִיתֶם קְדֹשִׁים (Leviticus 11:45) — and separated them from the impurity of foods and of semen in the impurity of the menstruant, and from the afflictions that derive from it, and from the impurity of the zavah and the impurity of sins, as He said מִכֹּל חַטֹּאתֵיכֶם לִפְנֵי ה׳ תִּטְהָרוּ (Leviticus 16:30), and from association with demons and the spirit of impurity, and from the impurity of forbidden relations, as He said אַל תִּטַּמְּאוּ בְּכָל אֵלֶּה (Leviticus 18:24) — He now says that the intent of all these admonitions is that they be holy, and this is so that they resemble their Maker as far as possible, just as was the intent in the creation of man, as He said נַעֲשֶׂה אָדָם בְּצַלְמֵנוּ כִּדְמוּתֵנוּ (Genesis 1:26). And this He now explains in His saying:" "<b>For holy am I, YHWH your Elohim.</b> And it is fitting that you resemble Me as far as possible, in thought and in deed. And to attain this resemblance, He explained that one must observe the commandments written in the first tablet, whose entire intent is for eternal life alone, as He explained at their conclusion in His saying לְמַעַן יַאֲרִיכוּן יָמֶיךָ, as was explained in its place. And He began to explain the matter of honoring father and mother, and said:"], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:56.234696362Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}